Background:
    Given I am logged in as a Platform Administrator
    And I am on the User management page

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator searches and filters users
    When I filter by role "Verifier"
    Then I should only see users with the role "Verifier"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator filters users by organization
    When I filter by organization "Trees 4 Hope"
    Then I should only see users belonging to "Trees 4 Hope"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator invites a new user
    When I click "Invite user"
    And I enter an email 
    Then the user should appear with status "Pending invite"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator changes a user's role
    Given I have selected user "Jane Mwanga"
    When I change her role to "Org manager"
    Then her role badge should update to "Org manager"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator suspends a user
    Given I have selected user "Lilian Kato" with status "Active"
    When I change her status to "Suspended"
    Then she should no longer be able to log in
    And her status should show "Suspended"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator reactivates a suspended user
    Given I have selected user "Lilian Kato" with status "Suspended"
    When I change her status to "Active"
    Then she should regain access
    And her status should show "Active"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator edits organization membership
    Given I have selected user "Jane Mwanga"
    When I check the "ECOTRUST" organization membership box
    Then "Jane Mwanga" should be added as a member of "ECOTRUST"

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator views a user's recent activity
    Given I have selected user "Jane Mwanga"
    Then I should see her recent activity log

@skip
  Scenario: Platform Administrator impersonates a user
    Given I have selected user "Samuel Okello"
    When I click "Impersonate"
    Then I should be logged in as "Samuel Okello"
